WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.468
-Guys, like I mentioned before,

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.570
President Trump was nominated
for a Nobel Peace Prize today,

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:05.905
and he's so confident
he's gonna win,

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.741
he already has his acceptance
speech written out.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.210
In fact, earlier today,
he was practicing

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.245
in front of the mirror,
and we got the footage.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.613
Check it out.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:21.286
-Ladies and gentlemen of the
Nobel committee, what an honor.

00:00:21.286 --> 00:00:23.623
I love Barnes &amp; Nobel.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.691
Great toy section.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.859
Not sure about Barnes,
but I love Nobel.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:30.063
I don't know Barnes.
Met him once.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.465
But we're not here
to talk about Barnes, are we?

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:36.369
We're here to talk about me, the
winner of the Nobel Peace Prize.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:40.873
It's great to be here in
beautiful, fantastic Norway.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:43.809
We love Norway.
Don't we?

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:46.612
Love the "fuh-jords."

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:49.182
But you know who never
visited Norway, by the way?

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.183
Hillary.
Throwback to that.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:52.685
I'm playing
all the hits tonight, folks.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.387
All the hits.
Buckle up.

00:00:55.387 --> 00:00:58.424
I got to be honest, this award
came at the perfect time.

00:00:58.424 --> 00:00:59.826
For a second there,
I almost thought

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.360
I was doing a bad job
as president.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.929
Can you believe that?

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.997
But you're right --
I'm amazing.

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:07.933
And I deserve this award
for many reasons.

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:12.271
For one, I finally brought peace
between the Arabs and Jews.

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:16.810
We love the Jewish people, or as
I call them the Yo-semites.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.311
And now they're
getting along great

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.980
with the United Arab "Erimates."

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.582
Emirates?
United Arab Erima--

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:26.819
Until this morning, I thought it
was a European soccer team.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:27.887
We're currently
looking into that.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.789
Are we looking into it?

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.223
But what about education, folks?

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:33.659
Under my administration,
there have been so many books

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:37.563
written about me...
committing treason.

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:40.700
Michael Cohen wrote one,
John Bolton,

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.934
one of my hotter nieces.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:45.138
So many...jobs created.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:48.174
So many Showtime movies adapted.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.143
And then, of course,
my biggest triumph.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.879
Of course,
I'm talking about vitamin C.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:55.181
The nana.
The Big Ronie,

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:58.350
as many people refer to it,
coronavirus.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.087
And now folks are mad because
Bob Woodward --

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:03.490
Bob Woodward
has me on tape saying

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.591
I knew it would be deadly
back in February.

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:09.562
But to those folks,
I say, called it.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:10.696
Remember that.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:12.432
Big victory.
Big victory, folks.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:16.035
But this celebration
is bittersweet, folks.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.404
Let me just be clear --
[ Inhales sharply ] --

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:21.207
and let me just
clear my nose for a second.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:26.446
[ Exhales sharply ]

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.148
It's a sad day for America.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.618
I'm sure you've heard "Keeping
Up with the Kardashians"

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:35.220
is ending its run
as one of the greatest shows

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.723
in the history of broadcasting.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:39.492
No more Kim, no more Kris,

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.262
no more Khloe
with her sassy remarks.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:45.431
I wish them all well and invite
each and every one of them

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:48.534
to join my cabinet.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:51.371
Finally, to all the little boys
and girls out there

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.606
who want to be president,
but let's be honest,

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:56.175
some people say it should only
be boys -- I don't know.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:59.478
Some people say.
Some people say that.

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:01.713
To all the little boys,
let this be a reminder

00:03:01.713 --> 00:03:06.652
that you can cyberbully your way
to a Nobel Peace Prize.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:09.322
Just remember, be best.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:12.658
And if that's not working,
be a little less best.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:16.062
So, in conclusion,
peace in the Mideast,

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:18.430
"Keeping Up" is deceased,
and as always,

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.566
no ramps for my feets.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.602
Invisible mic drop.

